  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31404524",
      "title": "How Does Authentication Work?",
      "lectureOrder": 173,
      "videoOrder": 169,
      "sourceHash": "9f1bc2223ba3cf77e9201ff70902f96c43cd073bcfa6284c477464f3fd5fad84",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.14,
          "end": 5.96,
          "en": "So, how does authentication work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.96,
          "end": 9.47,
          "en": "Well, you have your app running on a mobile device and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.47,
          "end": 14.47,
          "en": "for authentication, you also need a backend, a backend API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 14.6,
          "end": 17.79,
          "en": "like the fire base dummy API we used before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.79,
          "end": 19.723,
          "en": "in the course or any other API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.67,
          "end": 23.41,
          "en": "You need a backend because on that backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.41,
          "end": 25.7,
          "en": "we wanna validate the credentials,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.7,
          "end": 28.37,
          "en": "the email and password entered by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.37,
          "end": 29.94,
          "en": "We can't do this on the phone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.94,
          "end": 31.67,
          "en": "because the user data is stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.67,
          "end": 34.32,
          "en": "in a database that is not part of the phone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.32,
          "end": 36.123,
          "en": "but instead on some backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.11,
          "end": 38.9,
          "en": "Therefore once a user fills",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.9,
          "end": 42.85,
          "en": "out a form, an authentication form, and enters his",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.85,
          "end": 46.73,
          "en": "or her email and password, those credentials are sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.73,
          "end": 49.95,
          "en": "to the backend API with the http request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.95,
          "end": 54,
          "en": "and then on the backend, those credentials are validated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54,
          "end": 56.345,
          "en": "So on the backend, the backend checks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.345,
          "end": 60.52,
          "en": "whether that is a valid email address that was registered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.52,
          "end": 63.56,
          "en": "and whether a valid password was entered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.56,
          "end": 66.85,
          "en": "Or, if a user is created for the first time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.85,
          "end": 70.48,
          "en": "the email will be validated if it is a valid email address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.48,
          "end": 72.36,
          "en": "and the password will be validated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.36,
          "end": 74.58,
          "en": "if it is long enough and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.58,
          "end": 77.46000000000001,
          "en": "And then a user is created, or if it was created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.46000000000001,
          "end": 81.47,
          "en": "before, we simply confirm that the credentials are correct.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.47,
          "end": 84.2,
          "en": "In addition, once the backend determines",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.2,
          "end": 86.11,
          "en": "that the credentials are correct,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.11,
          "end": 90.10300000000001,
          "en": "it also typically generates an authentication token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.13,
          "end": 93.97,
          "en": "Now this token is in the end, just a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.97,
          "end": 97.02000000000001,
          "en": "just a bunch of text, which is created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.02000000000001,
          "end": 101.4,
          "en": "and signed by the backend and which can't be faked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.4,
          "end": 104.1,
          "en": "And this token is sent back to the phone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.1,
          "end": 107.97,
          "en": "So this string can't be faked, which can only be verified",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.97,
          "end": 110.28,
          "en": "by the backend because it was created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.28,
          "end": 113.77000000000001,
          "en": "by the backend is sent back to the phone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.77000000000001,
          "end": 116.12,
          "en": "This token is important because on the phone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.12,
          "end": 120.463,
          "en": "we know that if we have a token, that validation succeeded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.463,
          "end": 123.08,
          "en": "and this token will be required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.08,
          "end": 127.13,
          "en": "for future http requests that might be sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.13,
          "end": 130.99,
          "en": "to the same backend to other resources",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.99,
          "end": 133.44,
          "en": "on the backend to other end points",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.44,
          "end": 137.46,
          "en": "of that API that might require authentication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.46,
          "end": 141.8,
          "en": "If a request would be sent to a protected API endpoint,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.8,
          "end": 144.22,
          "en": "this token would be added to the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.22,
          "end": 146.31,
          "en": "by the phone and the backend could then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.31,
          "end": 148.5,
          "en": "verify that it's a valid token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.5,
          "end": 152.94,
          "en": "and grant access for those future http requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.94,
          "end": 155.64,
          "en": "Therefore, this token is stored on the device",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.64,
          "end": 157.86,
          "en": "because then we have something that proves",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.86,
          "end": 161.22,
          "en": "that the user is logged in and we have that token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 161.22,
          "end": 166.22,
          "en": "for future http requests to potentially secure resources so,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.91,
          "end": 170.76,
          "en": "secured API endpoints. That's the theory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 170.76,
          "end": 173.29,
          "en": "And we're going to see all these different aspects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 173.29,
          "end": 176.403,
          "en": "in action throughout this course section now.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
